LinuxPlay 1.0.0 — Roylyl
GPL-3.0-or-later; see LICENSE.

LinuxPlay is a Linux adaptation of Roylyl/WinPlay. The WinPlay interface,
artwork, CarPlay receiver behavior and protocol implementation are retained.
Linux changes replace Windows platform bridges with BlueZ/RFCOMM,
NetworkManager, desktop display integration, safeStorage-backed encryption,
MPRIS system media integration and Linux application packaging.

CarPlay control, pairing, encryption, plist and HID implementation adapted from
Roylyl/MacPlay, based on f-io/LIVI (Lasse Heitgres and contributors).
Wireless iAP2 identification and handoff adapted from Roylyl/AndroidPlay,
based on shihabal3amri/DiPlay. Original source comments are retained.
See vendor/MacPlay-NOTICE and vendor/SOURCE-AUDIT.md.

No Apple endorsement or MFi certification is claimed. The bundled authentication
pair is included in source distributions and application packages. Users may
optionally import a replacement pair locally. Credentials
require separate redistribution authorization. MacPlay NOTICE traces historical
experimental credentials to DiPlay 0.2.6 APK; redistribution authorization remains
unestablished. GPL licensing of application code does not grant rights to
authentication credentials.

Electron (MIT), its embedded Node.js runtime and Chromium/FFmpeg retain the
license texts included with the Electron distribution. Production npm packages
retain their respective licenses; see vendor/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt.
The standalone Node.js runtime used by the receiver retains its bundled
copyrights and license terms in resources/node-LICENSE.
Python, BlueZ, NetworkManager and the desktop D-Bus service are system
dependencies supplied by the Linux distribution and are not bundled here.

The LinuxPlay icon follows the AndroidPlay/MacPlay/WinPlay icon design family
with Linux-specific artwork. Original WinPlay artwork remains in the source
tree as part of the migration history. Editable SVG source is included.
